Subject: [PATCH] bsps/riscv/esp32: clear the RTC watchdog flash-boot bit

The LP/RTC watchdog on C5, C6 and S31 uses bit 12 for flash-boot mode,
as defined by ESP-IDF's lp_wdt_reg.h / rtc_wdt_reg.h. Clearing bit 8
leaves that independent watchdog mode enabled after a cold boot, causing
RTC_WDT_SYS resets even with the normal enable bit cleared.

--- a/bsps/riscv/esp32/start/bspstart.c
+++ b/bsps/riscv/esp32/start/bspstart.c
@@ -302,7 +302,7 @@
   /* Unlock and disable LP WDT */
   WRITE_REG( LP_WDT_BASE, 0x18, 0x50d83aa1U );
   uint32_t lp_wdt = READ_REG( LP_WDT_BASE, 0x0 );
-  WRITE_REG( LP_WDT_BASE, 0x0, lp_wdt & ~( BSP_BIT32( 31 ) | BSP_BIT32( 8 ) ) );
+  WRITE_REG( LP_WDT_BASE, 0x0, lp_wdt & ~( BSP_BIT32( 31 ) | BSP_BIT32( 12 ) ) );
 
   /* Unlock and auto-feed super watchdog (SWD) on C6 */
   WRITE_REG( LP_WDT_BASE, 0x20, 0x50d83aa1U );
